{title: Thou, Who at Thy First Eucharist Didst Pray}
{artist: William H. Turton / William H. Monk}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: thou-who-at-thy-first-eucharist-didst-pray.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Thou_Who_At_Thy_First_Eucharist-Unde_Et_Memores)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Thou, who at Thy first Eucharist didst pray
[D]That [A7]all Thy [Em]Church might [A7]be [D]forever [A]one,
[D]Grant us at every Eucha[Bm]rist to [D]say
[D]With [G]longing [E7]heart and [F#m]soul, Thy [E7]will be [A]done.
[A]O [D]may we [A7]all [D]one [G]bread, one body [D]be,
[D]Through [A7]this [D]blest [A7]sac[Bm]ra[G]ment of [A7]uni[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]For all Thy Church, O Lord, we intercede;
[D]Make [A7]Thou our [Em]sad di[A7]vi[D]sions soon to [A]cease;
[D]Draw us the nearer each to [Bm]each, we [D]plead,
[D]By [G]drawing [E7]all to [F#m]Thee, O [E7]Prince of [A]Peace;
[A]Thus [D]may we [A7]all [D]one [G]bread, one body [D]be,
[D]Through [A7]this [D]blest [A7]sac[Bm]ra[G]ment of [A7]uni[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]We pray Thee too for wanderers from Thy fold;
[D]O [A7]bring them [Em]back, good [A7]Shep[D]herd of the [A]sheep,
[D]Back to the faith which saints be[Bm]lieved of [D]old,
[D]Back [G]to the [E7]Church which [F#m]still that [E7]faith doth [A]keep;
[A]Soon [D]may we [A7]all [D]one [G]bread, one body [D]be,
[D]Through [A7]this [D]blest [A7]sac[Bm]ra[G]ment of [A7]uni[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]So, Lord, at length when sacraments shall cease,
[D]May [A7]we be [Em]one with [A7]all [D]Thy Church a[A]bove,
[D]One with Thy saints in one un[Bm]broken [D]peace,
[D]One [G]with Thy [E7]saints in [F#m]one un[E7]bounded [A]love;
[A]More [D]blessèd [A7]still, [D]in [G]peace and love to [D]be
[D]One [A7]with [D]the [A7]Trin[Bm]i[G]ty in [A7]uni[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}
